WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:20.678
This is the Daily Karma. Today’s practice is karma: intention before action. Find a supported position. Let your eyes close, or rest gently on the painting.

2
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:42.263
Settle into a position that can support both ease and alertness. Relax the muscles around your eyes and let the day become quieter.

3
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:07.009
Place attention where breathing feels clearest: the nose, chest, or belly. Receive each breath without needing to hold on to it.

4
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:31.291
Karma begins with intention. Before an action becomes a result, it is a choice about what we place into the world.

5
00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:01.077
Imagine a single seed resting in dark soil. It does not rush toward the light. It receives water, warmth, and time, then responds.

6
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:30.170
Notice what your body is doing with these words. Soften around the eyes, the hands, and the belly. Keep only the effort needed to stay present.

7
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:58.356
Notice one intention beneath today’s effort. It may be to contribute, to learn, or to care. Let the intention become simple and honest.

8
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:25.009
I will leave some quiet here. You do not need to empty the mind. Notice what appears, release the story, and return to breathing.

9
00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:03.870
Still here. Still breathing. Nothing special needs to happen. This quiet awareness is already a useful way of meeting your life.

10
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:26.195
Choose one small action that matches your intention. A thoughtful reply. A patient beginning. A promise kept without needing recognition.

11
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:53.124
Return awareness to the room. Move slowly, keeping a trace of this steadiness with you. When ready, open your eyes. Thank you for practicing with Karma.
